@startuml fig10-live-updates
!include style.iuml
title Figure 10 (new): Live updates when another member changes the group (NFR 3, R11; A5)

actor "Member B\n(this phone)" as B
participant ":GroupDetailActivity" as UI
participant ":GroupViewModel" as VM
participant ":GroupRepository" as GR
participant ":TransactionRepository" as TR
participant ":Subscription" as SUB
participant "db : FirebaseFirestore" as DB
actor "Member A\n(another phone)" as A

B -> UI : open a group
UI -> VM : startLiveUpdates(groupId)
VM -> GR : observeGroup(groupId, onChange)
GR -> DB : groups/{groupId}: addSnapshotListener(\nchangesOnly(DocumentSnapshot::getMetadata, onChange))
GR --> VM : Subscription
VM -> TR : observeTransactions(groupId, onChange)
TR -> DB : groups/{groupId}/transactions: addSnapshotListener(\nchangesOnly(QuerySnapshot::getMetadata, onChange))
TR --> VM : Subscription
note right of VM
  onChange is the ViewModel's Runnable changed =
  () -> remoteChange.setValue(new Event<>(true)), the same
  for both listeners; the group listener covers renames,
  member changes and deletion
end note
DB --> SUB : first snapshot of each listener (already shown) → ignored
...
A -> DB : adds / edits / deletes an expense or settlement\n(or renames the group, changes its members, deletes it)
DB --> SUB : new snapshot (no pending local writes)
SUB -> VM : onChange.run()
note right of SUB
  a listener error (for example access lost
  after being removed) also runs onChange
end note
VM --> UI : remoteChange (Event)
UI -> UI : refreshAll(): load(groupId), then refresh() on every\ncreated tab; each reloads and recomputes history,\nbalances, summary and members (C3 unchanged)
UI --> B : updated screen without pulling to refresh
...
B -> UI : leave the screen
UI -> VM : onCleared() (when the activity finishes)
VM -> SUB : remove() on both subscriptions
SUB -> DB : ListenerRegistration.remove()

legend bottom left
New interaction (not in Project 2.2).
endlegend
@enduml
